course: dictionary
lesson: 1624
title: Which chestnut? Reading the clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «Chestnut» can be a nut, a tree, a colour, or a joke. «The sweet chestnuts were roasted at the winter market.» Roasted and market are your clues: this is the nut you can eat.
explain: «Her chestnut hair shone in the sunlight.» Hair is not a nut or a tree, so chestnut must describe a colour. Test it by swapping in your meaning: "reddish-brown hair shone in the sunlight" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «An old chestnut» does not mean something very old. If someone says it about a story, the clue is the groan that follows: the joke has been told too many times. When the clues are unclear, check a dictionary.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Chestnut» can mean a nut, a tree, a reddish-brown colour, or a joke that has been told too many times.
fact: Sweet chestnuts can be roasted and eaten, but horse chestnuts are not for eating.
fact: A horse chestnut leaf is made of five to seven leaflets, like the fingers on a hand.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The sweet chestnuts were roasted at the winter market.» What does chestnut mean here? | A tree in the park | *A shiny reddish-brown nut you can eat | A reddish-brown colour | A joke told too many times
exercise: Find the meaning of chestnut in «Her chestnut hair shone in the sunlight.» | A horse chestnut conker | *A reddish-brown colour | A tree with five leaves | A nut in a prickly case
exercise: Ruby says, «That's an old chestnut», and the class groans. What does it mean? | *A joke or story told too many times | A chestnut tree that is very old | A brown horse | A very old nut
test: How many leaflets make up a horse chestnut leaf? | Two | Twenty | Three | *Five to seven
test: «Horse chestnuts are not for eating, but sweet chestnuts can be roasted.» Which chestnut can be roasted and eaten? | *Sweet chestnut | Horse chestnut | Chestnut hair | An old chestnut
exam: In «The chestnut tree dropped its prickly cases onto the path», what does chestnut mean? | A reddish-brown colour | A nut you can eat from a market stall | *A tree | A joke told too many times
